lesson k-what-the-wind-moves v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=6 subject=physics levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "What the wind moves"
  goal "Say what the wind, moving air, can push."

  look {
    scene 8x9 {
      windsock s wind=1 stripes=5 at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
        Wind is air moving. We cannot see air, but we can see what it moves: leaves, kites, washing and
        this windsock. A strong wind holds the windsock straight out; a light wind lets it droop.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.wind-moves k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.wind-moves count=3 seed=2 easy-count=2 hard-count=2
    show k.windsock-strong w=1 hard-w=0
    show k.see-the-wind k=1 easy-k=0
    show k.blow-further k=1 easy-k=0
    show k.make-a-pinwheel
    show k.windsock-strong w=0 hard-w=1
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.windy-washing
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.windier-day k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  remember {
    say "Wind is moving air. We see it by what it moves."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud. Push and pull showed a hand moving things; this lesson is the step on
    from it, air doing the pushing. The pinwheel is for you to watch. If the child is stuck, blow
    through a straw at a feather together. Off the page, fly a kite or a plastic bag on a string on
    a windy day. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines), 環境, 内容 (4):
    "自然などの身近な事象に関心をもち，取り入れて遊ぶ。" (Take an interest in familiar things in nature, and
    bring them into play.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level a kite is worked in the teacher's pen first, the things are light or very heavy, the questions ask whether wind can be seen and blow a feather, and the windier day is plain."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the wind moves a paper boat and washing, and the windier day is close."
  }
}
